-- title:
--   Automorphisms of y² = x³ - x in characteristic 3
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field with decidable equality and of characteristic $3$, and let $i \in K^{\times}$ satisfy $i^2 = -1$. Write $E_0$ for the Weierstrass curve with coefficients $(a_1,a_2,a_3,a_4,a_6) = (0,0,0,-1,0)$, i.e. $y^2 = x^3 - x$, and for a variable change $\gamma = (u,r,s,t)$ let $\gamma$ act on the points of the associated affine curve by sending the point at infinity to itself and $(x,y)$ to $(u^{-2}(x-r),\,u^{-3}(y-t-s(x-r)))$, a point of $\gamma \cdot E_0$ (so equalities with endomorphisms of $E_0(K)$ are stated as heterogeneous equalities). The assertion is that there exist additive endomorphisms $\alpha, \beta$ of the group of affine points of $E_0$ such that: $\alpha$ computes the action of $(i,0,0,0)$ and $\beta$ that of $(1,1,0,0)$; $\alpha(\alpha T) = -T$, $\beta(\beta T) + \beta T + T = 0$ and $\alpha(\beta T) = \beta(\beta(\alpha T))$ for all $T$; every variable change $\gamma$ with $\gamma \cdot E_0 = E_0$ acts on points as $m$ or as $-m$ for some $m$ among $\mathrm{id}, \alpha, \beta, \beta \circ \beta, \alpha \circ \beta, \alpha \circ \beta \circ \beta$; and conversely each of these six endomorphisms is the action of some variable change fixing $E_0$.
--
--   This is the explicit description of the automorphism group of the supersingular curve $y^2 = x^3 - x$ over a field of characteristic $3$ containing a square root of $-1$: it is generated by $[i]$ and the order-three automorphism $(x,y) \mapsto (x-1,y)$ special to characteristic $3$, with $\pm 1$ acting trivially on subgroups so that only six maps occur modulo sign. It is used in the characteristic-three computations of orders of $q$-expansions and modular-curve censuses, and in the transport statement for curves of $j$-invariant $0$ in characteristic $3$.
